auspice renown. Otherwise Pure have nothing to rip off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T09:09:41-07:00","id":850602,"title":"","content":"I think we had an entire thread about whether the first dot of renown is immediate, and if not how long does it take to set in and a whole bunch of other issues a while ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:01:09-07:00","id":850640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/849635-wolfblooded-with-gift-facets?p=850547#post850547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm of the idea your auspice afforded your first dot of auspice renown. Otherwise Pure have nothing to rip off.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean besides auspice ability, hunter's aspect, potentially the Moon Kuruth Trigger, and any Auspice-specific Merits?<br /> <br /> For the record, I agree with the interpretation that a werewolf gets their first dot in their Auspice Renown when they get their Auspice (which doesn't happen immediately after First Change, but will happen pretty quickly after unless the Pure find them first), but that's far from the only benefit joining the Pure strips a werewolf of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-21-2016, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:06:14-07:00","id":850643,"title":"","content":"Does this have anything to do with a wolf-blooded with a dot of Auspice Renown and equivalent Facet and the penalty one would receive for such a Tell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:07:43-07:00","id":850645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/849635-wolfblooded-with-gift-facets?p=850602#post850602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we had an entire thread about whether the first dot of renown is immediate, and if not how long does it take to set in and a whole bunch of other issues a while ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't recall it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:09:13-07:00","id":850646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/849635-wolfblooded-with-gift-facets?p=850640#post850640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean besides auspice ability, hunter's aspect, potentially the Moon Kuruth Trigger, and any Auspice-specific Merits?<br /> <br /> For the record, I agree with the interpretation that a werewolf gets their first dot in their Auspice Renown when they get their Auspice (which doesn't happen immediately after First Change, but will happen pretty quickly after unless the Pure find them first), but that's far from the only benefit joining the Pure strips a werewolf of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The rite in question worked by slicing off the renown brands, which is why they look crimson in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:14:15-07:00","id":850650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/849635-wolfblooded-with-gift-facets?p=850646#post850646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rite in question worked by slicing off the renown brands, which is why they look crimson in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worked being the keyword. We don't know how it will work in 2e. And like I said, I do agree that you get your first auspice renown when you get your auspice, I was just pointing out that there are a lot more benefits to be removed than just the renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:15:49-07:00","id":850652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/849635-wolfblooded-with-gift-facets?p=850650#post850650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Worked being the keyword. We don't know how it will work in 2e. And like I said, I do agree that you get your first auspice renown when you get your auspice, I was just pointing out that there are a lot more benefits to be removed than just the renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about benefits, I'm talking about literally ripping something off. I'm talking about symbolism. And while shit isn't published, the old material takes precedence, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T13:50:21-07:00","id":850791,"title":"","content":"*Ahem*<br /> <br /> People, please - fork off a new thread. The question I've asked hasn't been fully answered.<br /> <hr /><br /> Anyway:<br /> <br /> I wonder if a good way of doing it would just be giving the Wolf-Blooded <i>permission</i> to purchase a dot of Renown... as long as they <i>earn</i> it (with all the inherent problems of trying to do so with a flimsy human body). And the Spirits are watching.<br /> <br /> The real question is, of course, which Gifts they can pick from...<br /> <br /> Perhaps:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Great Things</b></span><br /> Your sleep is weird - restless and filled with dreams of running and fighting. They seem to quiet down a bit in places with the right &quot;feel&quot; - you only regain Willpower from rest when in an area Resonant to a particular type of Influence, chosen upon gaining this Tell.<br /> <b>Boon:</b> Your sleep is preparing you for great things - you can purchase a single dot of one Renown once you've performed an appropriate deed. You gain all the normal benefits for possessing a dot of Renown; the Facet you gain is drawn from a Gift appropriate for the Resonance you can sleep in. Note that many Facets are useless unless you happen to possess an additional Tell.<br /> <br /> It might be a tad limited unless you're taking it as a second Tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T07:04:54-07:00","id":851720,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting Tell you got. Though I have an alternative interpretation, maybe two. What if the Wolfblooded had one dot of Renown by default, and he could raise it with Experience? And in exchange, they suffer from a persistent Ban tied to the Renown the player picks?<br /> <br /> That way, not only do you enjoy the benefits of Renown when it comes to interacting with (or fighting) spirits in terms of Honorary Rank. But (if you want) each dot of Renown you purchase lets you earn Facets in a Wolf Gift?<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, I've been trying to work out a Tell which allows for a Wolf-Blooded to learn the Facet/s of a Shadow Gift. Of course, I've been having similar problems with how some Facets are useless without certain Tells and/or Werewolf traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}